          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-navy mb-6 leading-snug" data-i18n="qa.q3.question">
            How will you make Bastrop County better?
          </h2>

          <div class="prose prose-lg text-near-black/85 font-sans leading-relaxed space-y-4">
            <p data-i18n="qa.q3.p1">
              To me, making the county better starts with getting the basics right. People want roads they can drive on, deputies who can respond when they're needed, dependable emergency services, and a county government that spends their money wisely. The new ESD 3 started offering ambulance service on October 1st.
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="qa.q3.p2">
              They also want to know we're planning for growth instead of playing catch-up year after year. I believe in listening to people, but listening is only the beginning. You've got to put a plan together, fund it, get the work done, and be willing to answer for the results. That's how I'd judge whether we're making progress.
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="qa.q3.p3">
              We also formed the first County Health Department, a service greatly needed. This was the first county health department formed in the State of Texas in almost 50 years.
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="qa.q3.p4">
              I also served as the Court's liaison with a group of volunteers who worked diligently to be approved for a grant that will provide fiber broadband countywide. It was an approximately $54 million grant through the state.
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="qa.q3.p5">
              I served on the committee for the new Judicial Center, and we have purchased 27 acres to build a new courthouse. There are other improvements to be announced very soon.
            </p>
